From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: Register Source components with directory key paths.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Windows Optional v15 x64/i686 publishes Source4 for an Optional component
with a directory key path after UI Source selection. Once UI component
flags are reset correctly, Wine skips its registration because no File
key path exists, publishing Advertised1 instead.

Register its resolved source folder using Wine's existing source-marker
format. Disk zero is an internal no-file marker: no File sequence binds a
directory key path to Media. This does not claim Windows registry bytes
were measured. Public Get/publish values are measured. File key paths keep
the existing code. Close component keys on both no-file early exits.

Apply after msi-executeaction-ui-selection-transfer.patch. Only msi.dll.
Shared v15 Optional and mixed regressions are in the test-only artifact.

--- a/dlls/msi/action.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/action.c
@@ -3508,8 +3508,30 @@
                 WCHAR base[MAX_PATH];
                 LPWSTR sourcepath;
 
-                if (!comp->KeyPath || !(file = msi_get_loaded_file(package, comp->KeyPath)))
+                if (!comp->KeyPath)
+                {
+                    WCHAR *directory = msi_resolve_source_folder( package, comp->Directory, NULL );
+                    WCHAR *registered;
+                    SIZE_T length;
+
+                    /* Directory key paths have no File/Media sequence. Use the
+                     * source marker with disk zero, followed by their folder. */
+                    if (!directory) { RegCloseKey( hkey ); return ERROR_OUTOFMEMORY; }
+                    length = wcslen( directory ) + 4;
+                    if (!(registered = malloc( length * sizeof(WCHAR) )))
+                    { free( directory ); RegCloseKey( hkey ); return ERROR_OUTOFMEMORY; }
+                    swprintf( registered, length, L"00\\%s", directory );
+                    msi_reg_set_val_str( hkey, squashed_pc, registered );
+                    free( registered );
+                    free( directory );
+                    RegCloseKey( hkey );
                     continue;
+                }
+                if (!(file = msi_get_loaded_file(package, comp->KeyPath)))
+                {
+                    RegCloseKey( hkey );
+                    continue;
+                }
 
                 if (!(row = MSI_QueryGetRecord(package->db, L"SELECT * FROM `Media` WHERE `LastSequence` >= %d "
                                                              "ORDER BY `DiskId`", file->Sequence)))
